# Backups & debris — a copy of a live file must never be committed.
# Committed variants of these sat inside frontend/src/ and the frontend root,
# shadowing the live files they were copied from. Dated suffixes are covered too
# (`*.backup-*`, `*.before-*`), and `.run/` plus `screenshots/` hold runtime
# state and PNG evidence that do not belong in a commit's diff.
*.bak
*.backup-*
*.before-*
.run/
screenshots/

# Installer backups and superseded trees. These were tracked in full (47 files
# across 12 directories); each one is a dated copy of a live file. The content is
# in git history, so these are recovery points, not sources — never re-add them.
.hermesha-*-backups/
.hermesha-*-installed
.hl-chat-*-backups/
.hl-chat-*-rescue-*/
Hermes_Life_HL-CHAT-*_Patch_Packet/

# Every virtualenv, not just the exact name ".venv": three dead ones
# (.venv-broken, .venv-broken-gayzer, .venv-lenovo-backup, 447 MB) were invisible
# to git only because a venv ships its own .gitignore containing "*".
.venv*/
